-- title:
--   Separation of ℂ-points by values of sections
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a scheme (in the bottom universe) and let $f : G \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}$ be a separated morphism. A $\mathbb{C}$-point of $G$ is taken here in the form of an element of `SchemeHomOver (𝟙 (Spec (CommRingCat.of ℂ))) f`, that is, a morphism $\varphi : \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C} \to G$ together with a proof that $\varphi$ followed by $f$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}$. Given two such points $x \neq y$, the assertion is that there exist open subschemes $U, V$ of $G$, proofs that the preimage $x^{-1}U$ is the whole of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}$ and likewise $y^{-1}V$ (so $x$ factors through $U$ and $y$ through $V$), finite sets $fsU \subseteq \Gamma(G,U)$ and $fsV \subseteq \Gamma(G,V)$ of sections, and a real $\varepsilon > 0$, with the following property: for every $\mathbb{C}$-point $P$ of $G$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}$ that factors through both $U$ and $V$, it is impossible that simultaneously $\lVert \varphi(P) - \varphi(x)\rVert < \varepsilon$ for all $\varphi \in fsU$ and $\lVert \psi(P) - \psi(y)\rVert < \varepsilon$ for all $\psi \in fsV$; the value of a section at a $\mathbb{C}$-point is its image under the restriction map `appLE U ⊤` followed by the isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}, \mathcal{O}) \cong \mathbb{C}$ given by `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, and $\lVert\cdot\rVert$ is the absolute value on $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the Hausdorff separation property of the set of $\mathbb{C}$-points of a separated $\mathbb{C}$-scheme for the topology generated by the values of local sections: two distinct points admit basic neighbourhoods, cut out by finitely many sections and one $\varepsilon$, with no common $\mathbb{C}$-point. It feeds the construction of neighbourhoods of $\mathbb{C}$-points used in [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finset_forall_pointEquiv_eq_coe_mem_ball_of_differentiableOn_appLE_of_isSeparated`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finset_forall_pointEquiv_eq_coe_mem_ball_of_differentiableOn_appLE_of_isSeparated).
